            {'type': 'heading', 'text': 'Reading the Timeline'},
            "ACPWB's records show no visible effect from the October 8 and October 9 strikes: its overnight readers arrived on schedule both nights. On the night of October 10, they did not, and the timing is the part ACPWB's analysts keep coming back to. The overnight surge normally begins at 23:00 UTC. The first drone alert in the Vladimir region came at 3:51 a.m. Moscow time, which is 00:51 UTC. By then, ACPWB's readers had been missing for nearly two hours.",
